---
import SolutionPage from '../../layouts/SolutionPage.astro';
import TwoPathsCTA from '../../components/TwoPathsCTA.astro';
import MiniTwoPaths from '../../components/MiniTwoPaths.astro';
---

<SolutionPage

  compact={true}  title="Testosterone Therapy & Hormone Optimization for Men"
  parent="Muscle"
  oneliner="Testosterone replacement therapy (TRT) and full-panel hormone optimization — because low testosterone is just one piece of a much bigger hormonal picture."
  slug="hormones"
  description="Low testosterone affects most men over 40 but goes untested and untreated. My4MLife connects men to testosterone therapy, TRT evaluation, and complete men's hormone replacement through our contracted licensed telemedicine practice."
>
  <TwoPathsCTA
    otcProductName="ArmorVita Nutraceutical"
    otcDescription="D3 + K2 + Boron + Astaxanthin — pharmaceutical-grade foundational hormonal support. Supports testosterone-adjacent pathways without a prescription."
    otcCtaLabel="Order ArmorVita →"
    otcCtaHref="/cart?sku=armorvita-sub"
    rxDescription="Full hormone panel review (Total T, Free T, estradiol, TSH, cortisol AM, DHEA-S, SHBG), TRT evaluation, peptide hormone support, GLP-1 candidacy, and your complete personalized 4M protocol — through our licensed telemedicine partner."
    whenOtc="Fatigue and energy issues are present but you have no clinical low-T diagnosis and want a foundational starting point."
    whenRx="Persistent low-T symptoms — fatigue, low libido, brain fog, loss of muscle mass — and you want a full lab panel with TRT or peptide protocol if indicated."
    protegeFooter="Become a Protégé — daily protocol guidance, weekly coaching, hormone tracker →"
  />

  <h2 id="why-matters">Why this matters</h2>
  <ul class="why-list">
    <li>Hormonal decline after 35 degrades muscle, fat distribution, libido, mood, and brain speed simultaneously</li>
    <li>Elevated estradiol silently suppresses testosterone signaling even when total T looks borderline</li>
    <li>No training or nutrition protocol reaches its ceiling inside a hormonally depleted system</li>
  </ul>

  <MiniTwoPaths otcLabel="Order ArmorVita" otcHref="/membership" prompt="Ready to act?" />

  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Testosterone rarely crashes alone. Thyroid, cortisol, DHEA, and estradiol all
    degrade in parallel after 35 — compounding each other's effects on energy, body
    composition, and cognition. Low T is a symptom of a broken hormonal environment,
    not a standalone diagnosis.
  </p>

  <figure class="scene-figure">
    <img src="/images/scenes/hormones-labs.jpg" alt="Blood collection tubes — full hormone panel as the foundation of any optimization protocol" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>Guessing is the insulting behavior. Measuring is the beginning of optimization.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <MiniTwoPaths otcLabel="Order ArmorVita" otcHref="/membership" prompt="Don't accept the slow drift:" />

  <aside class="four-m-touchpoints">
    <h3>How ArmorVita touches all 4 Ms</h3>
    <div class="four-m-grid">
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Mind</span><p>Vitamin D is a steroid hormone with receptors throughout the brain. Astaxanthin is one of the few antioxidants powerful enough to cross the blood-brain barrier.</p></div>
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Muscle</span><p>D3 and Boron support testosterone — the upstream hormone behind muscle preservation, recovery, and lean mass.</p></div>
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Mitigate</span><p>K2 routes calcium to bones and away from arteries (arterial calcium drives most heart disease). D3 modulates immune function and inflammation across every system.</p></div>
      <div class="four-m-card"><span class="four-m-label">Motivate</span><p>Energy. Mood (seasonal affective disorder is largely vitamin D). Libido (testosterone). The sense of vitality men assume they've lost permanently.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="lifetime-usage">
      <h4>Why you'll want this for life</h4>
      <p>Your skin's ability to make vitamin D from sunlight drops about 50% by age 70. Modern indoor life cuts effective sun exposure by another 80%. Most men over 40 are clinically deficient and don't know it. Testosterone declines about 1% per year after 30 — without active support, the line goes one direction only. ArmorVita doesn't just fix a deficiency — it maintains a system that gets harder to maintain every year. Stop at 50 and the system you built collapses faster than it took to build.</p>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <p>These habits actively suppress your hormonal function every single day.</p>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>No baseline lab work in the past 2 years — flying blind on your own biology</li>
    <li>Chronic sleep deprivation under 7 hours — testosterone is produced during deep sleep</li>
    <li>Excess visceral body fat — fat tissue converts testosterone to estrogen</li>
    <li>Daily exposure to endocrine disruptors: plastics, fluoride, common pesticide residues</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="read-more-line">
    <a href="/blog/eliminate-the-insulting-behavior-hormones" class="read-more-link">
      Read the full deep-dive: Eliminate the Insulting Behavior — Hormones &rarr;
    </a>
  </p>

  <MiniTwoPaths otcLabel="Order ArmorVita" otcHref="/membership" prompt="OTC or Rx — pick now:" />
</SolutionPage>

<style>
.why-list {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0.5rem 0 1.75rem;
}
.why-list li {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  align-items: flex-start;
  padding: 0.5rem 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  color: var(--text);
  font-size: 0.97rem;
}
.why-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.why-list li::before {
  content: "✓";
  color: var(--accent);
  font-weight: 700;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  margin-top: 2px;
}
.read-more-line {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
}
.read-more-link {
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--primary-light);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.read-more-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
